⬇️FULL RECIPE⬇️
263 calories 23g protein (for the entire pint, toppings/mix-ins included)

Baked Alaska Protein Ice Cream 😋🍦

Original recipe from my Recipe Book

Check out the link in my bio for my Creami Recipe Books with over 140 recipes like this one!

- 400g Fat Free @fairlife Milk
- 40-45g @Lakanto Monk Fruit Sweetener
- 5g (1 tsp) vanilla bean paste (or extract)
- A pinch of salt
- 1g (¼ tsp) xanthan gum
Mix-ins/Toppings:
- 10g mini lucky-charms-style marshmallows (I used the ones from @jetpuffed)
- 15g white chocolate chips mixed with 2g of coconut oil
• Right before the Mix-In cycle, combine 15g of white chocolate with 2g of coconut oil, melt in the microwave (30 sec intervals, stirring in between), hollow out a hole in the center of the base, and pour in. After spinning on the Mix-In setting, it’ll turn into perfect, creamy chocolate chips.
263 cal 29g C, 6g F, 23g P

Instructions:
1. Blend all ingredients for the base and freeze (at least 16 hours)
2. Run your pint under hot water for at least 60 seconds
3. Spin on “Lite Ice Cream” setting
4. Spin on “Respin” setting (if powdery)
5. Make a hole down to the bottom with a butter knife and fill with the melted white chocolate and ¾ of your mini marshmallows
6. Run the “Mix-in” cycle
7. Top with the rest of the marshmallows

